# A10 — fixtures that run on the PG18 leg. PG is the primary contract:
# default expectation is EVERY fixture lands here; leaving one out
# needs a comment saying why.
port.select_implicit.sql
port.subquery_correlated_agg.sql
orig.spg_jsonb_at_op.sql
# orig.mysql_family_literals excluded: `"abc"` is an IDENTIFIER on this
# leg, which is PostgreSQL's rule and the very difference the fixture
# measures. Running it here would assert that PG is MySQL.
# orig.mysql_introducers excluded: PostgreSQL has no introducer syntax
# (`_utf8mb4'x'`), so every line is a parse error there.
# orig.mysql_session_collation excluded: `SET NAMES` sets the client
# ENCODING on this leg, not a collation, so there is no session
# collation for it to change and the fixture would assert nothing.
